cff-version: 1.2.0
message: "If you use this corpus, please cite it."
title: "PURSUE UAP Release Corpus"
abstract: >-
  A structured index of a Department of War / PURSUE initiative UAP
  declassified document and media release. 211 documents across 8,661 pages
  and 112 catalogued video files, indexed into a fixed six-layer spine that
  records what the documents say and where they say it, with page-level
  citations throughout. Absence is recorded rather than explained,
  contradictions are preserved side by side rather than reconciled, and
  extracted entities are marked as pattern candidates rather than verified
  facts. Coverage gaps are published alongside the data: 1,719 pages carry no
  text layer and 818 fall below the OCR confidence floor, so a null result can
  be told apart from an unread page.
type: dataset
authors:
